#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Vibepollo Installer & Updater — numeric releases with Stable/Latest selection, SHA-256 verification and rollback.

Installs or updates Vibepollo (https://github.com/Nonary/Vibepollo) on Windows and on Arch Linux
and Arch-based distributions (EndeavourOS, CachyOS, Manjaro, SteamOS). Upstream's Linux beta ships
only an x86_64 pacman package. Debian, Fedora, AppImage, and Flatpak builds are not published, so
this tool refuses to install on those distros instead of pretending a package exists.

- Uses GitHub release metadata (not tag naming) to distinguish time-gated Stable from Latest.
- Lists every release, pre-releases included, so any specific version can be installed (`--list`, `--install-version`).
- Linux: matches the official x86_64 Arch package (`vibepollo-*-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst`), installs via
  `pkexec pacman -U` (GUI) or `sudo pacman -U` (CLI), caches in `~/.cache/vibepollo-updater/`.
- Windows: matches the official `VibepolloSetup*.exe`, backs up `config` first, runs the installer
  elevated (one UAC prompt), caches in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\vibepollo-updater\\cache\\`.
- Verifies the GitHub-attested SHA-256 digest before installing (refuses on mismatch).
- Keeps the last 3 verified packages cached for 1-click rollback.
"""
